  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Molarity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Volume</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8201;</mi><mi>strength</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>.2</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11.2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>11.2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math><mn>1</mn></math> molar means <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi></math> solution contains&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8201;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#8201;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>34</mn><mi>&#8201;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p>Since, the strength is represented as weight of the solute in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> of the solution. The strength of the solution will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>34</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>Note: The question should&#39;ve mentioned that we need to find the mass by volume percentage.</p><p>Percentage w/v&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math></p>"
  }
